{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-1","title":"2 Samuel 7:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Nathan, first approving the purpose of David to build God a house, 4 after by the word of God forbids him. 12 God promises him benefits and blessings in his seed. 18 David's prayer and thanksgiving.</p>\n<p>the king. 1Ch 17:1-15; Da 4:29,30 the Lord. Jos 21:44; 23:1; 1Ki 5:4; 2Ch 14:6; Ps 18:1; *title Pr 16:7; Lu 1:74,75</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-2","title":"2 Samuel 7:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Nathan. 12:1; 1Ch 29:29 I dwell. 5:11; 1Ch 14:1; Jer 22:13-15; Hag 1:4 the ark. Ps 132:5; Joh 2:17; Ac 7:46 curtains. 6:17; Ex 26:1-14; 40:21; 1Ch 16:1; 2Ch 1:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-3","title":"2 Samuel 7:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Go, do. 2Ki 4:27 all that. 1Sa 16:7; 1Ki 8:17,18; 1Ch 22:7; 28:2; Ps 20:4; 37:4 for the. 1Sa 10:7; 1Jo 2:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-4","title":"2 Samuel 7:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>that night. Nu 12:6; 1Ch 17:3; Am 3:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-5","title":"2 Samuel 7:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>my servant David. Heb. to my servant, to David. Shalt. 1Ki 5:3; 8:16-19; 1Ch 17:4; 22:7,8; 23:3-32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-6","title":"2 Samuel 7:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>I have not. Jos 18:1; 1Ki 8:16; 1Ch 17:5,6 walked. Ex 33:14,15; 40:35-38; Le 26:23,24,27,28; Nu 10:33-36; De 23:14 2Co 6:16; Re 2:1 tent. Ex 40:18,19,34; Ac 7:44</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-7","title":"2 Samuel 7:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>walked. Le 26:11,12 any of the tribes. 1Ch 17:6 any of the judges.Instead of [shbty,] {shivtey,} \"tribes,\" we should probably read, with Houbigant, Drs. Waterland and A. Clarke, and others, [shpty,] {shophtey,} \"judges;\" which is the reading in the parallel passage. Indeed there is but one letter of difference between them, and letters which might be easily mistaken for each other; the apex under the upper stroke of the [p,] {pay,} being the only mark to distinguish it from the [b,] {baith.} Compare with ver. 11.</p>\n<p>feed. 5:2; Ps 78:71,72; Isa 40:11; Jer 3:15; 23:4; Eze 34:2,15,23 Mic 5:4; Mt 2:6; *marg: Joh 21:15-17; Ac 20:28; 21:28; 1Pe 5:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-8","title":"2 Samuel 7:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>I took thee. 1Sa 16:11,12; 1Ch 17:7; Ps 78:70 following. Heb. after. ruler. 6:21; 12:7; 1Sa 9:16; 10:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-9","title":"2 Samuel 7:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>And I was. 5:10; 8:6,14; 22:30,34-38; 1Sa 18:14; 1Ch 17:8 cut off. 22:1; 1Sa 31:6; Ps 18:37-42; 89:23 out of thy sight. Heb. from thy face. a great. Ge 12:2; 1Sa 2:8; 1Ch 17:8; Ps 113:7,8; Lu 1:52 like unto. Ps 87:3-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-10","title":"2 Samuel 7:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>plant them. 1Ch 17:9; Ps 44:4; 80:8; Jer 18:9; 24:6; Eze 37:25-27; Am 9:15 neither. Ps 89:22,23; Isa 60:18; Eze 28:24; Ho 2:18; Re 21:4 as beforetime. Ex 1:13,14,22; Jud 4:3; 6:2-6; 1Sa 13:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-11","title":"2 Samuel 7:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>since. Jud 2:14-16; 1Sa 12:9-11; Ps 106:42 have caused. 1; Job 5:18,19; 34:29; Ps 46:9 he will make. 27; Ex 1:21; 1Ki 2:24; 11:38; 1Ch 17:10; 22:10; Ps 89:3,4; 127:1 Pr 14:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-12","title":"2 Samuel 7:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>And when. 1Ki 2:1; 8:20 sleep. De 31:16; 1Ki 1:21; Da 12:2; Ac 13:36; 1Co 15:51; 1Th 4:14 I will set. Ge 15:4; 1Ki 8:20; 1Ch 17:11; Ps 89:29; 132:11,12; Isa 9:7 Isa 11:1-3,10; Mt 22:42-44; Ac 2:30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-13","title":"2 Samuel 7:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>He shall. 1Ki 5:5; 6:12; 8:19; 1Ch 17:11,12; 22:9,10; 28:6,10; Zec 6:13 Mt 16:18; Lu 1:31-33; Heb 3:3; 1Pe 2:5 I will stablish. 16; 1Ch 28:7; Ps 89:4,21,29,36,37; Isa 9:7; 49:8; Lu 1:32,33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-14","title":"2 Samuel 7:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>I will be. 1Ch 17:13; 28:6; Ps 89:20-37; Mt 3:17; Heb 1:5 If he. Ps 89:30-35 I will. De 8:5; Job 5:17; Ps 94:12,13; Pr 3:11,12; Jer 30:11; 1Co 11:32 Heb 12:5-11; Re 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-15","title":"2 Samuel 7:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>But my. 14,16; 1Sa 19:24; Ps 89:28,34; Isa 55:3; Ac 13:34-37 as I took. 1Sa 15:23,28; 16:14; 1Ki 11:13,34-36; Isa 9:7; 37:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-16","title":"2 Samuel 7:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>13; Ge 49:10; 2Ki 19:34; 1Ch 17:13,14; Ps 45:6; 72:5,17-19 Ps 89:36,37; Isa 9:7; Da 2:44; 7:14; Mt 16:18; Lu 1:32,33 Joh 12:34; Heb 1:8; Re 11:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-17","title":"2 Samuel 7:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>1Ch 17:15; Ac 20:20,27; 1Co 15:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-18","title":"2 Samuel 7:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>sat. 1Ch 17:16; Isa 37:14 Who am I. Ge 32:10; Ex 3:11; Jud 6:15; 1Sa 9:21; 15:17; 18:18; Ps 8:4; Eph 3:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-19","title":"2 Samuel 7:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>And this. 12:8; Nu 16:9,13 but thou. 11-16; 1Ch 17:17 And is this. Ps 36:7; Isa 55:8,9; Eph 2:7; 3:19,20 manner. Heb. law.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-20","title":"2 Samuel 7:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>knowest. Ge 18:19; 1Sa 16:7; Ps 139:1; Joh 2:25; 21:17; Heb 4:13; Re 2:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-21","title":"2 Samuel 7:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>thy word's. Nu 23:19; De 9:5; Jos 23:14,15; Ps 115:1; 138:2; Mt 24:35 Lu 1:54,55,72 according. Mt 11:26; Lu 10:21; 12:32; 1Co 1:1; Eph 1:9; 3:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-22","title":"2 Samuel 7:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Wherefore. De 3:24; 1Ch 16:25; 2Ch 2:5; Ps 48:1; 86:10; 96:4; 135:5; 145:3 Eze 36:22,32 none. Ex 15:11; De 4:35; 32:39; 1Sa 2:2; Ps 86:8; 89:6,8; Isa 40:18,25 Isa 45:5,18,22; Jer 10:6,7; Mic 7:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-23","title":"2 Samuel 7:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>what one. De 4:7,8,32-34; 33:29; Ps 147:20; Ro 3:1,2 went. Ex 3:7,8; 19:5,6; Nu 14:13,14; Ps 111:9; Isa 63:7-14; Tit 2:14 1Pe 2:9; Re 5:9 make him. Ex 9:16; Jos 7:9; 1Ch 17:21; Isa 63:12,14; Eze 20:9; Eph 1:6 great things. De 10:21; Ps 40:5; 65:5; 66:3; 106:22; 145:6 thy people. De 9:26; 15:15; Ne 1:10 nations and their gods. Ex 12:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-24","title":"2 Samuel 7:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>confirmed. Ge 17:7; De 26:18 art become. 23; Ex 15:2; De 27:9; 1Ch 17:22; Ps 48:14; Isa 12:2; Jer 31:1,33 Jer 32:38; Ho 1:10; Zec 13:9; Joh 1:12; Ro 9:25,26; 1Pe 2:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-25","title":"2 Samuel 7:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>establish it. Ge 32:12; Ps 119:49; Jer 11:4,5; Eze 36:37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-26","title":"2 Samuel 7:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>let thy. 1Ch 17:23,24; 29:10-13; Ps 72:18,19; 115:1; Mt 6:9; Joh 12:28 before thee. Ge 17:18; 1Ch 17:23,24; Ps 89:36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-27","title":"2 Samuel 7:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>revealed. Heb. opened the ear. Ru 4:4; 1Sa 9:15; *marg: Ps 40:6 I will. 11 found. 1Ch 17:25,26; Ps 10:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-28","title":"2 Samuel 7:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>thy words. Nu 23:19; Joh 17:17; Tit 1:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2sa-7-29","title":"2 Samuel 7:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2SA","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>let it please thee to bless. Heb. be thou pleased and bless. Nu 6:24-26; 1Ch 17:27; Ps 115:12-15 for ever. 22:51</p>"}]}